The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
static void __exit etnaviv_exit(void)
{
    // Missing platform_device_unregister(etnaviv_drm);
    platform_driver_unregister(&etnaviv_platform_driver);
}
```
Reason:
The `etnaviv_exit()` function does not call `platform_device_unregister()` to unregister the `etnaviv_drm` device when the module is removed. This oversight causes the device to remain registered, leading to a duplicate filename error in sysfs when the module is reloaded.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
static void __exit etnaviv_exit(void)
{
    platform_device_unregister(etnaviv_drm);
    platform_driver_unregister(&etnaviv_platform_driver);
    platform_driver_unregister(&etnaviv_gpu_driver);
}
```
Reason:
The addition of `platform_device_unregister(etnaviv_drm);` in the `etnaviv_exit()` function ensures that the device is properly unregistered when the module is removed, preventing the duplicate filename error in sysfs upon reloading the module.

